Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: enable the Z8803BE WAN jack LED

The existing pinctrl already routes the WAN PHY's LED0 to the jack.
Expose that LED under /sys/class/leds for LuCI/netdev control.
LED1 stays disabled: the physical jack has a single orange indicator.
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7988a-zbtlink-zbt-z8803be.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7988a-zbtlink-zbt-z8803be.dts
@@ -306,6 +306,13 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&i2p5gbe_led0_pins>;
 };
 
+&i2p5gbe_led0 {
+	color = <LED_COLOR_ID_AMBER>;
+	function = LED_FUNCTION_WAN;
+	linux,default-trigger = "netdev";
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &switch {
 	status = "okay";
 };
